---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
---
<DocsLayout title="Introduction" headings={[]} source="site/src/pages/index.astro">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Edit model weights with Python</h1>
    <p class="lead">Access named tensors, evaluate your changes, and save a standalone checkpoint.</p>
    <Code code={`python3 -m pip install -e 'packages/python[editing]'`} lang="bash" />
    <Code code={`from wsm import WeightModel

model = WeightModel.load("/path/to/snapshot")
model.weights["model.norm.weight"][:16].mul_(0.95)
result = model.evaluate([{"prompt": "Say hello.", "target": "Hello!"}])
model.save("/path/to/checkpoint")`} lang="python" />
    <p>To run a file, define <code>edit(model)</code> and execute it with the CLI.</p>
    <Code code={`mkdir -p runs
wsm execute edit.py --model /path/to/snapshot --cases examples/coding/cases.json --output runs/edit`} lang="bash" />
    <p>The runner records baseline and candidate evaluations. You decide whether to keep the change. Python executes with your process privileges.</p>
    <p><a href="/docs/coding/">Read the Python editing guide</a> or <a href="/docs/quickstart/">Start building</a>.</p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
